best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","great","best","best","excellent","great"],"moments":[{"ply":39,"name":"20.Qxh6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"20.Qxh6!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the knight on h5 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 20…gxh5 21.Qxh5 Nf8 22.h4 the engine rates it 0.00.","Takes the pawn on h6.","The queen joins the attack: it now hits 4 squares around the Black king.","20.Qxh6 threatens Qg7#, with mate in 1.","It threatens Qg7#, with mate in 1, so Black has to spend the next move on it."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"20.Qxh6!! ignores the attack on the knight on h5 and takes the h6 pawn first. Taking the knight still leaves White level."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"The knight on h5 is attacked by the g6 pawn, and 20.Qxh6 doesn't save it. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the knight","text":"20…gxh5 is met by 21.Ng5, threatening Qh7+ and mate. Then 22.Qxg5+ gives check, and 24.Rf3 threatens Qxh5, winning a pawn. White is a piece down: White holds the balance (+0.43). This is Black's best try."}]},{"ply":42,"name":"21…Bxg5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"21…Bxg5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on g5.","The next best move, 21…Nf8, would drop Black's winning chances from 50% to 39% (+1.19).","21…Bxg5 stops the mate threat Qh7+.","White was threatening Qh7+, with mate in 2. Bxg5 takes care of it.","Trades bishop for knight.","The bishop on g5 can be taken by the queen on h6."]},{"ply":53,"name":"27.Qg5+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"27.Qg5+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked queen to safety.","Shores up the e5 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 2).","The next best move, 27.Qg3, would drop White's winning chances from 42% to 31% (−2.22).","27.Qg5+ saves the attacked queen.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","Black answers 27…Ke8."]},{"ply":57,"name":"29.Qg5+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"29.Qg5+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked queen to safety.","Shores up the e5 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 2).","The next best move, 29.Qg7, would drop White's winning chances from 43% to 27% (−2.68).","29.Qg5+ saves the attacked queen.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","Black answers 29…Ke8."]}],"opening":{"name":"French Defense, Classical, 4. Bg5","eco":"C12","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9.O-O: 17 moves in all, 9 by White and 8 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9.O-O: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}